Grouping of a bunch of K04564 matching sequences across Alveotata genomes, with
some genomes contributing multiple copies on different sequencing contigs. I
also included the 11 transcript sequences here. I was able to narrow down to 3
groups: a) SP+cTP like - this includes 8 of the 11 transcript protein
sequences, b) SP likely - includes 3 of the transcript protein sequences, and
c) One mTP, with the leader called mTP by both DeepLoc and TargetP.

Observations
  * The PF00081 and PF02777 regions of the sequences look distinct,
    between the 3 groups
  * The leader sequence of the SP+cTP group appears to have conservation
  * The SP group leaders are less conserved, but n is smaller

Reference panel and alignment

We assembled a metal-labeled Fe/Mn-SOD reference panel of sequences
(ref_metals.faa) and retrieved cofactor annotations from UniProt. See
k04564_metal_scores.tsv for sequence metal preferences (label column).  Only 3
of the sequences are experimentally supported (all Fe: E. coli SodB P0AGD3,
Arabidopsis FeSOD1 P21276, rice FeSOD2 Q5VSB7); the remainder, including every
Mn reference, are curator annotations, so the Mn pole of the scale is
annotation-anchored, not assay-anchored. 

The labeled references were aligned into one 366-column frame together with
K04564 alveolate sequences (27 SP/cTP, 9 SP, 1 mTP), giving a shared coordinate
system in which homologous metal-discriminating positions can be compared
directly across groups.

Scoring and conclusions. Rather than importing literature column numbers, we
learned the Fe-vs-Mn discriminant positions from the labeled references
themselves — 9 columns where well-occupied Fe and Mn references carry different
majority residues — and validated the discriminant before applying it: it
correctly classifies 11/12 Fe references (negative score) and 22/22 Mn
references (positive), and the columns it recovered include the canonical
second-shell discriminants (col 143 Gln-Fe/Gly-Mn; col 222 Ala-Fe/Gln-Mn),
confirming the signal is the known structural fingerprint and not a dataset
artifact.

Scored on this validated scale, all three K04564 groups fall on the Mn side:
SP/cTP mean +0.78 (as Mn-like as the Mn references), mTP +0.89, and SP +0.38
(Mn-leaning but weaker, with 3 members near the midline). The interpretation,
held to the 80% threshold: by residue signature these are putative Mn-type SODs
(confidence ~85% that the sequences are Mn-type; ~70% that they load Mn in
vivo, since sequence signature and actual metal occupancy can diverge in
cambialistic SODs). Notably, the metal signal does not track the leader
grouping — the SP/cTP and SP groups are ~50% divergent in their mature domains
(distinct protein lineages) yet both read Mn-like, so the groups differ in
targeting and in sequence lineage but not in predicted metal.
